        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "996aa235-1ea8-56d6-aa79-496df2c795ea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: 41st Tactical Squadron, 41st Air Tactical Squadron, German Luftwaffe, Mikoyan design bureau\n- Places: 22nd Air Base, Soviet Union\n- Products: Mikoyan MiG-29, Sukhoi Su-27, McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle, General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon\n- Concepts: air superiority fighter, NATO reporting name\n\nFacts:\n- The Mikoyan design bureau developed the Mikoyan MiG-29 in the Soviet Union during the 1970s as an air superiority fighter.\n- The Mikoyan MiG-29 was developed alongside the Sukhoi Su-27 to counter the McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle and the General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon.\n- The Mikoyan MiG-29 is a twin-engine jet fighter aircraft, and its NATO reporting name is Fulcrum.\n- The 41st Tactical Squadron operates Mikoyan MiG-29 jet fighters acquired from the German Luftwaffe.\n- The 41st Air Tactical Squadron is the main unit based at the 22nd Air Base and flies MiG-29 fighters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
